	title 'Print Manager--AppleTalk Driver   Verison 3.1'*******************************************************************	      The Print Manager*	 Apple Talk Port Driver  v3.1*** Original Code by Luc Barthelet and Versionsoft.* Summer, Fall and Winter 1986** Rewritten by Steven E. Glass* March 13, 1987** Version 1.0      Apr 10, 1987	Steven E. Glass** Version 1.1      May 7, 1987	Steven E. Glass & Suki Lee *    Error checking	is done in all routines and passed back	to*    caller via completion routine. ** Version 1.2      Jun 19, 1987	Suki Lee*    DevOpen no longer calls PapInit based on warning from*    Greg Seitz. PapInit should only be	called by ATInit at*    system start up. We could have potentially reinitialized*    all file servers on the network.*    DevOpen, DevClose, DevRead, DevWrite and DevStatus has*    been rewritten	to follow AppleTalk	rules.** Version 2.0d1    Nov 25, 1987	Harry Yee** Version 2.0d2    Dec 03, 1987	Harry Yee*    Parameter block for appletalk call	GetInfo changed.*    Call DevStartup puts together the network name a little differently due to*    a change in the printer drivers reverting back to the way PrChanged*    was originally	called in the 1.2 drivers.** Version 2.1      Aug 4, 1988	Suki Lee*    Added timer to	time out on async write if it does not return. If the printer*    is in an error	state, e.g. out of paper, paper jam, an	async write will not*    return since it has not completed.	We force a return if the timer expires*    before the write completion.** Version 2.1d2    Aug 14, 1988	Steven Glass*    The DevRead made a PapRead call without setting the first*    word of the parameter table.  If the last call*    made was an ASyncRead, it will still be set this way.*    we fixed this by always writing the read code into the*    parameter table.**    There was a bug in the DevAsyncRead call.  This routine*    checks for a completion vector and if it is zero uses*    a sync read call.  But the code wrote the async code into*    the write param block.** Version 3.0d1    Nov 17, 1988	Suki Lee*    The AppleShare Programmer's Guide for the IIGS states that the flow quantum *    parameter in the PAPOpen param block should always be 1. This value indicate*    the number of 512 byte buffers. For whatever reason, ours is set to 8. The*    code works fine now since the current PAPOpen ignores what's passed and*    always sets it to 1, according to Tim Harrington. But for future compatibility, *    this value should be set to 1 in our param block.**    Added code to return end of file flag from a PAPRead in DevAsyncRead's*    completion routine. This value is returned in Y. ** d2               Dec 2, 1988          Suki Lee*    The new ROM has AppleTalk in slots 1 or 2, freeing up slot 7. The IsItSafe*    routine is modified to check ROM verison and look at the appropriate slot   *    to determine if AppleTalk is turned on in the control panel.* * d3               Dec 16, 1988         Suki Lee*    Added new header to denote this as a driver which will support new calls.*    This header is 2 words long: first word is 0 followed by a call count word.** d4               Jan 16, 1989         Suki Lee*    Removed 3 calls, GetZoneList, GetPrinterList and GetMyZone, that are no longer*    used since the Choose Printer functionality has been moved to the Control Panel.*    Added code to return 0 in A for DevPrChanged and DevStartUp and return the result*    from PAPStatus call in DevStatus.** d5               Apr 17, 1989	Suki Lee*    AppleTalk PAP for printers is designed so that when an open is received, it waits*    2 seconds for other opens, if any, and then accepts the one which has been waiting*    the longest. During this time, the printer will not accept any other type of PAP *    commands. The user may decide to cancel the print job at this early stage, so we *    need to build in a 2 second wait loop to disallow closing of the connection during*    that window.* * Version 3.1d1    Dec 15, 1989	Suki Lee*    Increased 2 second timer to 3 seconds for a work around to bug in AppleTalk Option*    Card.** 3.1d2 (?)	6-Apr-92	Mark Day*    Changed the algorithm used to see if AppleTalk is on.  It now checks for the*    presence of the AppleTalk main driver.  This should make it work with the*    EtherTalk card.  Changed returned version number to 3.1.** (branch)	24-Jul-92	Mark Day*    Testing out a quick little hack: DevOpen copying the session refnum immediately*    after making the PAPOpen.  I moved it until after its 3 second delay.  It's too*    bad that it doesn't actually wait for the open to complete....** 3.1d9	29-Jul-92	Dave Lyons and Mark Day*    Removed dead code & cleaned up GetTick calls (uses subroutine GetTickA).*    Changed PrDevOpen to wait forever for the PAPOpen to complete, or until*      they hit Command-Period.  Always retries on $0808 error (server too*      busy to respond).  Retries ten times on $0805 error (name not found).*    Changed PrDevWrite to wait forever for the PAPWrite to complete, or*      until they hit Command-Period.**    If you equate Debugging to 1, you get the following run-time breaks to*    step over when things go wrong:*       BRK $81   A = error coming back from DevStatus*       BRK $82   A = error coming back from DevOpen*       BRK $83   A = error coming back from DevRead*       BRK $84   A = error coming back from DevWrite*       BRK $85   A = error coming back from DevClose*       BRK $86   A = error coming back from DevAsyncRead*       BRK $87   IsItSafe is returning False**       Also, the border color does funky psychadelic things while the*       ShouldWeKeepWaiting routine keeps waiting.** 25-Mar-93 DAL** Made DevStatus keep trying on an $0808 error (Server Not Responding).******************************************************************Debugging	equ 0*******************************************************************	 Copyright 1986-1993*	 Apple Computer, Inc.*	 All Rights Reserved******************************************************************	include 'all.macros'	include 'special.macros';------------------------------------------;; Equates from procedure AppleTalkPort;;------------------------------------------VersionNb	equ $0302	; Version 3.2 (2-Apr-93 SS)NetNameLength	equ 99NameLength	equ 33EntrySize	equ NameLength+5	; 5 bytes needed by	list managerNoError1	equ 0	; No errorPortNotOn	equ $1302	; Port not activeTrue	equ $FFFFFalse	equ $0000Temp1	equ 0Init	equ $01RegisterName	equ $0ERemoveName	equ $0FLookUpName	equ $10ConfirmName	equ $11pTemp	equ $0;-----------------------------------------------;;   Imports;;-----------------------------------------------	IMPORT AlertTemp320	IMPORT AlertTemp640;-----------------------------------------------;;   Forward addresses and entries;;-----------------------------------------------	ENTRY ChoosedName	ENTRY CopyString	ENTRY DATA	ENTRY DevAsyncRead	ENTRY DevClose	ENTRY DevIsItSafe	ENTRY DevOpen	ENTRY DevPrChanged	ENTRY DevRead	ENTRY DevShutDown	ENTRY DevStartup	ENTRY DevStatus	ENTRY DevWrite	ENTRY DevWriteBackGround	ENTRY Device	ENTRY EofRead	ENTRY EofWrite	ENTRY exit0	ENTRY exit4	ENTRY Exit6	ENTRY Exit8	ENTRY Exit10	ENTRY IsItSafe	ENTRY Marker	ENTRY OurOpenCompletion	ENTRY OurReadCompletion	ENTRY OurWriteCompletion	ENTRY PapCloseParms	ENTRY PapOpenParms	ENTRY PapReadParms	ENTRY PapStatusBuff	ENTRY PapStatusParms	ENTRY PapWriteParms	ENTRY PrPortVer	ENTRY ReadAdrBuf	ENTRY ReadBuffer	ENTRY ReadLength	ENTRY ResultClose	ENTRY ResultOpen	ENTRY ResultRead	ENTRY ResultWrite	ENTRY SessionRefClose	ENTRY SessionRefOpen	ENTRY SessionRefRead	ENTRY SessionRefWrite	ENTRY StatusBuffer	ENTRY StatusResult	ENTRY WriteAddress	ENTRY WriteBuffer	ENTRY WriteLength	ENTRY Zone	entry ShouldWeKeepTrying	entry myEventRecord,myEventMessage,myEventModifiers******************************************************************* Port Drivers start with a jump table.	 The call number comes* in the x-register	and is used to index into the jump table.******************************************************************AppleTalkPort	PROC;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Header to denote new calls supported;	DC.W 0	; marker	DC.W (EndProcList-ProcList)/4 ; count of calls supported	jmp (ProcList,x)	EXPORT ProcListProcList	DC.L DevPrChanged	DC.L DevStartup	DC.L DevShutDown	DC.L DevOpen	DC.L DevRead	DC.L DevWrite	DC.L DevClose	DC.L DevStatus	DC.L DevAsyncRead	DC.L DevWriteBackGround	DC.L PrPortVer	DC.L DevIsItSafe	EndProcList	ENDP;                copy Device*********************************	           ** Device	           **	           ** Current Rev.  Jun	11, 1987   **	           *********************************;--------------------------------------------------------------;; All the device calls which uses AppleTalk PAP calls has its; own completions routine which executes caller's completion; routine and loads	the returned result	code in the A register.; The pointer to the routine's completion routine is passed; as a parameter to	the PAP calls. The caller can check the; result code in the A register.;***************************************************************** PrPortVer ** Returns version #	of currently installed port****************************************************************	EXPORT PrPortVerPrPortVer	PROC	DefineStackOrigD	Word 0OrigB	Byte 0Rtl1	Block 3Rtl2	Block 3Version	Word 0	phd	tcd	phb	phk	plb	lda #VersionNb	sta Version,s	lda #0	plb	pld	brl exit0	ENDP****************************************************************** Deref** Space for pointer	    LONG* Handle for list	    LONG** Dereference handle and put pointer into Pointer****************************************************************	EXPORT DerefDeref	PROC	DefineStackorigD	wordRTSAdr	wordPointer	longHandle	long	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [Handle],y	sta Pointer+2	lda [Handle]	sta Pointer	pld	; restore direct page	rts	EndP******************************************************************* DevPrChanged********************************************************************	EXPORT DevPrChangedDevPrChanged	PROC	DefineStackOrigB	byteOrigD	wordRTLAdr1	block 3RTLAdr2	block 3DeviceType	long	phd	; for some reason we save D	phb	; save dbr	phk	; and set dbr to k	plb	tsc	tcd	lda DeviceType	clc	adc #2	; skip past first two bytes before	tax	; getting to the device name	lda DeviceType+2	adc #0	pha	phx	PushLong #Device	ldy #NameLength-1	jsr CopyString	lda Device	and #$00FF	inc a	clc	adc #Device	sta Zone	lda #^Device	adc #0	sta Zone+2	lda #0	plb	pld	brl Exit4	ENDP******************************************************************* DevStartup**     Pointer to Network Device Name** This is called at	PMStartup to tell this driver what the* network device is	to be.******************************************************************	EXPORT DevStartupDevStartup	PROC	DefineStackStartUp_DPage	word 0StartUp_BReg	byte 0StartUp_rtl1	block 3StartUp_rtl2	block 3Startup_ZoneName	long 0StartUp_PrinterName	long 0	jsr IsItSafe	bcc Yes	brl Exit8Yes		; 	phd	; save d	phb	; save dbr	phk	; set dbr to k	plb	tsc	tcd;----------------------------------------------------------;; Copy name into ChoosedName field in local data.;	PushLong Startup_PrinterName	PushLong #ChoosedName	lda [Startup_PrinterName]	and #$00FF	tay	jsr CopyString	lda [Startup_PrinterName]	and #$00FF	inc a	clc	adc #ChoosedName	sta Marker	lda #^ChoosedName	adc #0	sta Marker+2	PushLong #Device	PushLong Marker	lda Device	and #$00FF	tay	jsr CopyString	lda Device	and #$00FF	inc a	clc	adc Marker	sta Marker	lda Marker+2	adc #0	sta Marker+2	PushLong Startup_ZoneName	PushLong Marker	lda [Startup_ZoneName]	and #$00FF	tay	jsr CopyString	lda #0	plb	pld	brl Exit8	ENDP******************************************************************* DevShutDown** Does nothing.******************************************************************	EXPORT DevShutDownDevShutDown	PROC	jsr IsItSafe	brl Exit0	ENDP******************************************************************* DevOpen**      OpenCompletionPtr    LONG*      Reserved	        LONG******************************************************************	EXPORT DevOpenDevOpen	PROC	DefineStackDevOpen_DPage	word 0DevOpen_BReg	byte 0DevOpen_rtl1	block 3DevOpen_rtl2	block 3Reserved	long 0OpenCompletion	long 0	jsr IsItSafe	bcc Yes	brl Exit8Yes	phd	; save d	phb	; save dbr	phk	; set dbr to k	plb*** added 29-Jul-92 DAL/MSD -- retry the open on name-not-found ($0805) this many times	lda #10	sta OpenRetries*** end 29-Jul-92;--------------------------------------------------------------------;; EofWrite is the EOF flag for PAPWrite, it should be set ONLY when; the last Write is	issued. We do it in	PAPClose by issuing	a PAPWrite; with no data and the EofWrite set.;	sep #$20	stz EofWrite	rep #$20	stz CallersCompletion1 ; assume low word is zero	lda OpenCompletion+2,s ; look at OpenCompletion (high word	sta CallersCompletion1+2 ; set first word of pointer	ora OpenCompletion,s ; if NIL then do syncOpen	beq syncOpen	lda #$2380	; $23 is command code for PAPOpen	sta PapOpenParms	; $80 indicates async call	lda OpenCompletion,s ; now put low word	in.	sta CallersCompletion1	bra MakeCallSyncOpen		; 	lda #$2300	; $00 indicates synchronous call	sta PapOpenParmsMakeCall	_AppleTalk PapOpenParms	lda PAPOpenParms	cmp #$2300	; if sync, no need to wait	beq GoOn*** 29-Jul-92 DAL and MSD -- keep waiting unless the call completes or they want to abortKeepWaiting	lda ResultOpen	jsr ShouldWeKeepTrying	bcc KeepWaiting*** end 29-Jul-92GoOn*** added 29-Jul-92 DAL/MSD -- If it's $0808 (server not responding) keep trying	lda ResultOpen	cmp #$0808	beq MakeCall*** if error is $0805 (name not found) then keep trying, up to 10 times	cmp #$0805	bne @strangeError	dec OpenRetries	bne MakeCall@strangeError;; 24-Jul-92 MSD: This code had been just before the lda PAPOpenParms (i.e.; before the 3 second delay).  If the open was async, it's unlikely the refnum; was returned that fast.;*** get result now in case it becomes valid right after we try using the session ref	lda ResultOpen	pha	sep #$20	longa off	lda SessionRefOpen	sta SessionRefClose	sta SessionRefRead	sta SessionRefWrite	longa on	rep #$20	pla	;ResultOpen to return as error code                if Debugging then	beq @noOpenError	brk $82@noOpenError                endif	plb	pld	brl Exit8OpenRetries	dc.w 0	;retry on $0805 error until this gets down to zero	EXPORT CallersCompletion1CallersCompletion1	DS.B 4	EXPORT OurOpenCompletionOurOpenCompletion		;       	lda >CallersCompletion1 ; not an async call	ora >CallersCompletion1+2	beq SkipIt	lda >CallersCompletion1+1 ; execute the	caller's	pha	; completion routine.	phb	lda >CallersCompletion1	dec a	sta 1,s	lda >ResultOpen	; load returned result in ASkipIt	rtl	ENDP******************************************************************* DevRead**    Space for bytes transfered    WORD*    Ptr to buffer	               LONG*    Bytes to Transfer             WORD******************************************************************	EXPORT DevReadDevRead	PROC	DefineStackDevRead_DPage	word 0DevRead_BReg	byte 0DevRead_rtl1	block 3DevRead_rtl2	block 3ReadRqd	word 0PtrReadBuf	long 0readTrnsfrd	word 0	jsr IsItSafe	bcc Yes	brl Exit6Yes	phd	; save d	phb	; set b to k	phk	plb	lda PtrReadBuf,s	sta ReadAdrBuf	lda PtrReadBuf+2,s	sta ReadAdrBuf+2	lda #$2500	; force the parameters to be sync read	sta PapreadParms	_AppleTalk PapReadParms	lda ReadLength	; store actual length read in result	sta ReadTrnsfrd,s	lda ResultRead                if Debugging then	beq @noReadErr	brk $83@noReadErr                endif	plb	pld	brl Exit6	ENDP******************************************************************* DevWrite**      WriteCompletion routine     LONG*      Ptr to buffer               LONG*      length of buffer            WORD******************************************************************	EXPORT DevWriteDevWrite	PROC	DefineStackDevWrite_DPage	word 0DevWrite_BReg	byte 0DevWrite_rtl1	block 3DevWrite_rtl2	block 3WriteLengthS	word 0WritePtrBuff	long 0WriteCompletion	long 0	jsr IsItSafe	bcc Yes	brl Exit10Yes	phd	phb	phk	plb	stz CallersCompletion2 ; assume that no	completion 	lda WriteCompletion+2,s ; check for completion routine	sta CallersCompletion2+2	ora WriteCompletion,s	beq syncWrite	; none	lda #$2680	sta PapWriteParms	lda WriteCompletion,s	sta CallersCompletion2	bra MakeCallSyncWrite	lda #$2600	sta PapWriteParmsMakeCall	lda WritePtrBuff+2,s	sta WriteAddress+2	lda WritePtrBuff,s	sta WriteAddress	lda WriteLengths,s	sta WriteLength	_AppleTalk PapWriteParms*** 29-Jul-92 DAL and MSD -- This was boneheaded.  Try really hard to succeed.LoopWait	lda ResultWrite	jsr ShouldWeKeepTrying	bcc LoopWait*** end 29-Jul-92	lda ResultWrite                if Debugging then	beq @noWriteErr	brk $84@noWriteErr                endif	plb	pld	brl Exit10	EXPORT CallersCompletion2CallersCompletion2	DS.B 4	EXPORT OurWriteCompletionOurWriteCompletion	lda >CallersCompletion2	ora >CallersCompletion2+2	beq SkipIt	lda >CallersCompletion2+1	pha	phb	lda >CallersCompletion2	dec a	sta 1,s	lda >ResultWriteSkipIt	rtl	ENDP******************************************************************* DevClose**     No inputs.******************************************************************	EXPORT DevCloseDevClose	PROC	jsr IsItSafe	bcc Yes	brl Exit0Yes	phd	phb	phk	plb;--------------------------------------------------------------;; Set EofWrite to indicate this is the last Write to be issued.; Issues a PAPWrite	with no data to send only the EOF flag.; 	sep #$20	longa off	lda #$01	sta EofWrite	longa on	rep #$20	lda #$2600	sta PapWriteParms	stz WriteAddress+2	stz WriteAddress	stz WriteLength	_AppleTalk PapWriteParms;--------------------------------------------------------------;; Finally, make the	close call.	_AppleTalk PapCloseParms	lda ResultClose                if Debugging then	beq @noCloseErr	brk $85@noCloseErr                endif	plb	pld	brl Exit0	ENDP******************************************************************* DevStatus**    Pointer to Input Status Buffer	LONG******************************************************************	EXPORT DevStatusDevStatus	PROC	DefineStackDevStatus_DPage	word 0DevStatus_BReg	byte 0DevStatus_rtl1	block 3DevStatus_rtl2	block 3AppStatusBuffer	long 0	jsr IsItSafe	bcc Yes	brl Exit4Yes	phd	phb	phk	plb	lda AppStatusBuffer,s	sta PapStatusBuff	lda AppStatusBuffer+2,s	sta PapStatusBuff+2@tryAgain	_AppleTalk PapStatusParms*** added 25-Mar-93 DAL -- Be persistent!  I don't like those $0808 errors!	lda statusResult	cmp #$0808		;"Server Not Responding"	bne @not0808	lda #$00ff		;pretend it's not done	jsr ShouldWeKeepTrying	bcc @tryAgain*** end 25-Mar-93@not0808	lda statusResult                if Debugging then	beq @noPapError	brk $81@noPapError                endif	plb	pld	brl Exit4	ENDP******************************************************************* DevAsyncRead**     Actual length	read             WORD*     Ptr to completion routine      LONG*     How much to read               WORD*     Ptr to buffer	                 LONG******************************************************************	EXPORT DevAsyncReadDevAsyncRead	PROC	DefineStackAsyncRead_DPage	word 0AsyncRead_BReg	byte 0AsyncRead_rtl1	block 3AsyncRead_rtl2	block 3Buffer	long 0DataLength	word 0Completion	long 0ActualLength	word 0	jsr IsItSafe	bcc Yes	brl Exit10Yes	phd	phb	phk	plb	stz CallersCompletion3 ; assume that no	completion 	lda Completion+2,s	; check for completion routine	sta CallersCompletion3+2	ora Completion,s	beq syncRead	; none	lda #$2580	sta PapReadParms	lda Completion,s	sta CallersCompletion3	bra MakeCallSyncRead	lda #$2500	sta PapReadParms	; this was write SEG 14 Aug 88MakeCall	lda Buffer+2,s	sta ReadAdrBuf+2	lda Buffer,s	sta ReadAdrBuf	_AppleTalk PapReadParms;------------------------------------------------------------------;; Data from the next 3 lines of code are valid at this time	for; sync Reads only;	ldx ResultRead	;get the result first in case it's not done (29-Jul-92 DAL/MSD)	lda ReadLength	; store actual length read in result	sta ActualLength,s;;;	lda ResultRead	txa	;29-Jul-92 DAL/MSD                if Debugging then	beq @noReadErr	brk $86@noReadErr                endif	plb	pld	brl Exit10	EXPORT CallersCompletion3CallersCompletion3	DS.B 4	EXPORT OurReadCompletionOurReadCompletion		;       	lda >CallersCompletion3	ora >CallersCompletion3+2	beq SkipIt	lda >CallersCompletion3+1 ; put completion routines address	on	pha	; stack	phb	lda >CallersCompletion3	dec a	sta 1,s	lda >ReadLength	; put actual length in X-reg	tax	lda >EofRead	; put end of file flag in Y-reg	tay	lda >ResultRead	; put error code in	A-regSkipIt	rtl	; make call by executing RTL	ENDP******************************************************************* DevWriteBackground**      Pointer to CompletionProc	LONG*      Buffer Size		WORD*      Pointer to Buffer	LONG** This one does not	seem to be implemented.******************************************************************	EXPORT DevWriteBackgroundDevWriteBackground	PROC	jsr IsItSafe	bcc Yes	brl Exit10Yes	phd	phb	phk	plb	plb	pld	brl Exit10	ENDP***************************************************************** DevIsItSafe**    Output:  Safety    WORD    boolean** * EntryPoint to driver from outside.** Safety is true if	it is safe, false if not.* ***************************************************************	EXPORT DevIsItSafeDevIsItSafe	PROC	DefineStackRTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3Result	word	jsr IsItSafe	bcc Yes	lda #False	sta Result,sGetOut	lda #0	brl Exit0Yes	lda #True	sta Result,s	bra GetOut	ENDP***************************************************************** IsItSafe** Common routine to	see if the device we want to deal with* is switched in.** If it is safe, a-reg is set to zero and carry is clear.* If it is NOT safe, a-reg is set to error code and carry is*    set. * ***************************************************************	EXPORT IsItSafeIsItSafe	PROC	;; 6-Apr-92 MSD: Changed the algorithm used to determine whether AppleTalk; is installed and running.  The supported way is to check for the; presence of a device driver with deviceID = $1D.;AppleTalkMain	equ $001D	; AppleTalk main device driver deviceID	lda #1	; start with first device in listloop	sta >devNum	_DInfoGS DInfoPB	bcs noAppleTalk	; assume it was invalid device number		lda >deviceID	cmp #AppleTalkMain	beq yesAppleTalk	; we found it!		lda >devNum	ina	; try the next device	bra loopnoAppleTalk	sec	lda #PortNotOn	; error is port not turned on                if Debugging then	brk $87                endif	bra exityesAppleTalk	clc	lda #0	; no error, we found itexit	rtsDInfoPB	dc.w 8	; through deviceIDdevNum	dc.w 0	dc.l nameBuffer	; pointer to result buffer for name	dc.w 0	; characteristics	dc.l 0	; total blocks	dc.w 0	; slot number	dc.w 0	; unit number	dc.w 0	; versiondeviceID	dc.w 0nameBuffer	dc.w 35	; size of result buffer	dc.w 0	; actual size of name	ds.b 31	; room for name	;	pha;	pha;	pha;	pha	; 4 word spaces for result;	pha	; A reg value, don't care;	pha	; x reg value, don't care;	pha	; y reg value, don't care;	lda #$FE1F	; the entry point to a routine which;	pha	; returns system information;	_FWEntry;	pla	; Y register has ROM version;	plx	; get unused values off stack;	plx;	plx	;	and #$00FF	; in bits 7 - 0;	cmp #3	; Version 3 or greater has AppleTalk;	bge ROM3Plus	; in slots 1 or 2;	;	lda >$E0C02D	; Read slot state, lo byte has the info;	and #$0080	; bit 7 set means external;;	beq ExitSafe;NotOn	lda #PortNotOn	; set error to port	not turned on;	bra ExitNotSafe;	;ROM3Plus;	lda >$E101C0	; Read AppleTalk port location;	and #$00FF	; lo byte only;	beq NotOn 	; 0 means it's not on ;;ExitSafe		 ;	lda #0	; no problems;ExitNotSafe	cmp #1;	rts;;SafeError	DS.B 2	ENDP****************************************************************** PortAlert** Alert box to tell	user that the appropriate port is not turned* on.** no parameters on stack*****************************************************************	EXPORT PortAlertPortAlert	PROC	_InitCursor	; restore cursor back to arrow	pha	; make room for result	_GetMasterSCB	pla	pha	; make room for result of alert call 	and #$80	; check mode 	beq mode320	; 320 mode	pushlong #alerttemp640 ; use 640 mode template	bra GoOnmode320	pushlong #alerttemp320 ; use 320 mode templateGoOn	pushlong #$0000	_StopAlert;              jsr WaitCursor	; set to watch again	pla	; get the item hit off stack	rts	ENDP***************************************************************** Data* ***************************************************************	EXPORT DataData	PROC	EXPORT PapOpenParmsPapOpenParms		; 	DC.B $80	; sync flag  (modified in line	DC.B $23	; depending on call	EXPORT ResultOpenResultOpen	DC.W 0	DC.L OurOpenCompletion ; completion pointer	EXPORT SessionRefOpenSessionRefOpen	DC.B 0	EXPORT OpenNameOpenName	DC.L ChoosedName	DC.B 1	; indicates one 512 byte buffer	DC.L StatusBuffer	EXPORT PapReadParmsPapReadParms		; 	DC.B $00	; sync / async flag	DC.B $25	EXPORT ResultReadResultRead	DC.W 0	DC.L OurReadCompletion ; completion routine pointer	EXPORT SessionRefReadSessionRefRead	DC.B 0	EXPORT ReadLengthReadLength	DC.W 0	EXPORT ReadAdrBufReadAdrBuf	DC.L ReadBuffer	EXPORT EofReadEofRead	DC.B 0	EXPORT PapCloseParmsPapCloseParms		; 	DC.B $00	; synchronous	DC.B $24	EXPORT ResultCloseResultClose	DC.W 0	DC.L 0	EXPORT SessionRefCloseSessionRefClose	DC.B 0	EXPORT PapWriteParmsPapWriteParms		; 	DC.B $80	; sync / async flag	DC.B $26	EXPORT ResultWriteResultWrite	DC.W 0	EXPORT papWriteProcpapWriteProc	DC.L OurWriteCompletion ; completion pointer	EXPORT SessionRefWriteSessionRefWrite	DC.B 0	EXPORT WriteLengthWriteLength	DC.W 512	EXPORT WriteAddressWriteAddress	DC.L WriteBuffer	EXPORT EofWriteEofWrite	DC.B 0	EXPORT PapStatusParmsPapStatusParms		; 	DC.B $00	; sync	DC.B $22	EXPORT StatusResultStatusResult	DC.W 0	DC.L 0	; no completion pointer	EXPORT StatusNameStatusName	DC.L ChoosedName	EXPORT PapStatusBuffPapStatusBuff	DC.L StatusBuffer	EXPORT DeviceDevice	DS.B 65	; printers in a specified zone	EXPORT ZoneZone	DS.B 4	; contains address of where zone name;	            ; is to	go in NameLookup structure	EXPORT MarkerMarker	DS.B 4	EXPORT ChoosedNameChoosedName	DS.B 99	; contains the printer name, device name;		; and zone name. Used by the Appletalk;		; PAP calls to open	connection for;		; printing.	EXPORT StatusBufferStatusBuffer	DS.B 128	; Please keep the buffers	EXPORT ReadBufferReadBuffer	DS.B 512	; one after the other to	EXPORT WriteBufferWriteBuffer	DS.B 512+8	; let them used by lookup*** added 29-Jul-92 DAL	export myEventRecord,myEventMessage,myEventModifiersmyEventRecord	dc.w 0	;whatmyEventMessage	dc.l 0	;message	dc.l 0	;when	dc.w 0,0	;wheremyEventModifiers	dc.w 0	;modifiers*** end 29-Jul-92	ENDP;                copy DynamicExits	EXPORT DynamicExitsDynamicExits	PROC* in a Dynamic exit	we need to save 2 RTLs	EXPORT exit20exit20	tax	lda 5,s	sta 25,s	lda 3,s	sta 23,s	lda 1,s	sta 21,s	tsc	clc	adc #20	tcs	txa	brl exit0	EXPORT Exit16Exit16	tax	lda 5,s	sta 21,s	lda 3,s	sta 19,s	lda 1,s	sta 17,s	tsc	clc	adc #16	tcs	txa	brl Exit0	EXPORT Exit14Exit14	tax	lda 5,s	sta 19,s	lda 3,s	sta 17,s	lda 1,s	sta 15,s	tsc	clc	adc #14	tcs	txa	brl Exit0	EXPORT Exit12Exit12	tax	lda 5,s	sta 17,s	lda 3,s	sta 15,s	lda 1,s	sta 13,s	tsc	clc	adc #12	tcs	txa	bra Exit0	EXPORT Exit10Exit10	tax	lda 5,s	sta 15,s	lda 3,s	sta 13,s	lda 1,s	sta 11,s	tsc	clc	adc #10	tcs	txa	brl Exit0	EXPORT Exit8Exit8	tax	; Standard 8 bytes input exit	lda 5,s	sta 13,s	lda 3,s	sta 11,s	lda 1,s	sta 9,s	pla	pla	pla	pla	txa	brl Exit0	EXPORT Exit6Exit6	tax	; Standard 6 bytes input exit	lda 5,s	sta 11,s	lda 3,s	sta 9,s	lda 1,s	sta 7,s	pla	pla	pla	txa	brl Exit0	EXPORT Exit4Exit4	tax	; Standard 4 bytes input exit	lda 5,s	sta 9,s	lda 3,s	sta 7,s	lda 1,s	sta 5,s	pla	pla	txa	brl Exit0	EXPORT Exit2Exit2	tax	; Standard 2 bytes input exit	lda 5,s	sta 7,s	lda 3,s	sta 5,s	lda 1,s	sta 3,s	pla	txa	EXPORT Exit0Exit0	cmp #1	; Standard 0 byte input exit	rtl	ENDP;                copy utils.asm****************************************************************** CopyString** Input : Pointer To Source String*       : Pointer to Dest String** Ouput : none** Register Y contains the number of bytes to copy from the source* pointer to the destination ptr.*****************************************************************	EXPORT CopyStringCopyString	PROC	DefineStackOrigD	wordRTSAdr	wordDestPtr	LONGSrcPtr	LONG	phd	tsc	tcd	lda #0	sep #%00100000	longa offLoop	lda [SrcPtr],y	sta [DestPtr],y	dey	bpl Loop	rep #%01100000	longa on	longi on	pld	pla	plx	plx	plx	plx	pha	rts	ENDP****************************************************************** ShouldWeKeepTrying (jsr)** Input:*   A = error word from an async AppleTalk call, $xxFF if incomplete** Output:*   SEC if we are done (the call completed or the user wants to*       give up)*   CLC if we should keep waiting (call is not complete and user*       is being very patient and trusting)*****************************************************************ShouldWeKeepTrying	proc                if Debugging then	pha	sep #$20	longa off	lda >$e1c034	eor #$0f	sta >$e1c034	rep #$20	longa on	pla                endif	and #$00ff	;still going if low byte is $ff	cmp #$00ff	bne StopWaiting	pha	;space for EventAvail result	pea $0008	;keyDown mask	pushlong #myEventRecord	_EventAvail	pla	beq KeepWaiting	lda myEventMessage	and #$00ff	cmp #$002e	;Period	bne notCmdPeriod	lda myEventModifiers	and #$0100	;Command key	bne StopWaiting*** They pressed a key, but not Command-period.  Grab it so we can see a new key next time.notCmdPeriod	pha	pea $0008	pushlong #myEventRecord	_GetNextEvent	plaKeepWaiting	clc	rtsStopWaiting	sec	rts	EndP	END